      "violation_detail": "The call was extremely short (10 turns) and the agent ended it without exhausting any options. The customer's responses were confused, not a clear refusal or confirmation of identity. The agent did not attempt to bridge the conversation, explore the customer's situation, or provide any concrete reasons for payment. This constitutes a premature call ending. Rule 80 is critical and states that if the call is short and the agent did NOT exhaust all options (concrete bridges, credit impact, timeline exploration, escalation warning) before ending, score 1. A short call where the borrower was evasive or gave short answers is NOT a reason to end — the agent should have tried harder."
